// Title: Potential Persistence Via Disk Cleanup Handler - Registry
// ID: d4f4e0be-cf12-439f-9e25-4e2cdcf7df5a
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-21
// Tags: attack.persistence
// Description: Detects when an attacker modifies values of the Disk Cleanup Handler in the registry to achieve persistence.
// The disk cleanup manager is part of the operating system. It displays the dialog box […]
// The user has the option of enabling or disabling individual handlers by selecting or clearing their check box in the disk cleanup manager's UI.
// Although Windows comes with a number of disk cleanup handlers, they aren't designed to handle files produced by other applications.
// Instead, the disk cleanup manager is designed to be flexible and extensible by enabling any developer to implement and register their own disk cleanup handler.
// Any developer can extend the available disk cleanup services by implementing and registering a disk cleanup handler.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

source = logs-* | where ((EventType = "CreateKey" AND registry.path like "%\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer\\VolumeCaches\\%") AND NOT (((registry.path="*\\Active Setup Temp Folders" OR registry.path="*\\BranchCache" OR registry.path="*\\Content Indexer Cleaner" OR registry.path="*\\D3D Shader Cache" OR registry.path="*\\Delivery Optimization Files" OR registry.path="*\\Device Driver Packages" OR registry.path="*\\Diagnostic Data Viewer database files" OR registry.path="*\\Downloaded Program Files" OR registry.path="*\\DownloadsFolder" OR registry.path="*\\Feedback Hub Archive log files" OR registry.path="*\\Internet Cache Files" OR registry.path="*\\Language Pack" OR registry.path="*\\Microsoft Office Temp Files" OR registry.path="*\\Offline Pages Files" OR registry.path="*\\Old ChkDsk Files" OR registry.path="*\\Previous Installations" OR registry.path="*\\Recycle Bin" OR registry.path="*\\RetailDemo Offline Content" OR registry.path="*\\Setup Log Files" OR registry.path="*\\System error memory dump files" OR registry.path="*\\System error minidump files" OR registry.path="*\\Temporary Files" OR registry.path="*\\Temporary Setup Files" OR registry.path="*\\Temporary Sync Files" OR registry.path="*\\Thumbnail Cache" OR registry.path="*\\Update Cleanup" OR registry.path="*\\Upgrade Discarded Files" OR registry.path="*\\User file versions" OR registry.path="*\\Windows Defender" OR registry.path="*\\Windows Error Reporting Files" OR registry.path="*\\Windows ESD installation files" OR registry.path="*\\Windows Upgrade Log Files"))))
